\section{Claims}

\subsection{Primary Claim}

A sexual aid device comprising:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\alph*)]
\item An inner core constructed of highly flexible elastomeric material with hardness rating Shore A 5-10, said inner core having a diameter of 8-12mm and extending substantially the full length of the device;
\item A middle structural layer surrounding said inner core, constructed of semi-rigid elastomeric material with hardness rating Shore A 50-70, said middle layer having a thickness of 4-5mm and providing compression resistance while permitting flexion of said inner core;
\item An outer surface layer surrounding said middle structural layer, constructed of very soft elastomeric material with hardness rating Shore A 10-15, said outer layer having a thickness of 2-3mm and providing surface compliance;
\item Wherein said three-layer construction creates a biomimetic structure that permits dynamic flexibility through said inner core while maintaining penetrative rigidity through said middle structural layer, and wherein said outer surface layer provides realistic tactile properties.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Dependent Claims}

\textbf{Claim 2:} The device of Claim 1, wherein said inner core, middle structural layer, and outer surface layer are composed of platinum-cured silicone with varying durometer ratings.

\textbf{Claim 3:} The device of Claim 1, wherein said middle structural layer includes directional reinforcement such as embedded mesh or fibers to enhance hoop strength.

\textbf{Claim 4:} The device of Claim 1, wherein said device has an overall length of 15-20cm and diameter of 3-5cm.

\textbf{Claim 5:} The device of Claim 1, wherein said three layers are bonded through a multi-step molding process creating a unitary structure.

\section{Advantages Over Prior Art}

\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*]
\item \textbf{Biomimetic Flexibility}: Unlike conventional dual-density designs with firm cores, this invention allows natural articulation and conformance to anatomical contours through the flexible inner core.

\item \textbf{Maintained Structural Integrity}: The semi-rigid middle layer provides compression resistance and penetrative capability without creating the "rigid stick" feel of conventional firm-core designs.

\item \textbf{Realistic Surface Compliance}: The soft outer layer provides natural surface tactile properties independent of the internal structural support.

\item \textbf{Dynamic Response}: The three-layer architecture enables the device to flex, bend, and compress in biomimetically accurate ways while maintaining functional rigidity.

\item \textbf{Improved User Experience}: The combination of surface softness, structural support, and core flexibility more closely replicates natural biomechanical properties than any existing design.
\end{enumerate}

\section{Manufacturing Considerations}

\subsection{Materials}
All layers preferably constructed from platinum-cured medical-grade silicone with varying Shore A hardness ratings. Alternative elastomers may be substituted while maintaining the specified hardness relationships.

\subsection{Production Method}
Multi-step injection molding or casting process:
\begin{enumerate}
\item Form inner flexible core
\item Overmold middle structural layer
\item Overmold outer surface layer
\item Ensure chemical bonding between layers during curing
\end{enumerate}

